(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[2434],{13526:function(e,t,a){"use strict";a.d(t,{Z:function(){return n}});var s=a(85893),o=a(85215);a(1717);var r=a(67294);function n(e){let{src:t}=e,a=(0,r.useRef)();return(0,r.useEffect)(()=>{a.current&&(0,o.Z)(a.current,{poster:"https://369cdn.com/video/".concat(t,".jpg"),sources:[{src:"https://369cdn.com/video/".concat(t,".mp4")}]})},[t]),(0,s.jsx)("video",{controls:!0,ref:a,className:"video-js vjs-16-9"})}},96501:function(e,t,a){"use strict";var s=a(85893),o=a(9295),r=a(13526),n=a(4229);t.Z=[{title:"Get started with crypto",subtitle:"Learn how to get started by buying your first ETH",slug:"crypto",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["Getting started with cryptocurrency is easy! Simply follow these two steps:",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"1. Get a wallet"}),"You have the choice between using the ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://metamask.io/download",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"MetaMask.io"})," browser extension or HEXscout as your cryptocurrency wallet.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Important: During the setup process, your wallet will show you a Secret Recovery Phrase. It's crucial that you write down these 12 words with a physical pen, on two separate pieces of paper, and store them in two different locations. Never show them to anyone else or create a digital copy. Protecting your Secret Recovery Phrase is crucial for keeping your cryptocurrency safe.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)(r.Z,{src:"HEXscout_How_to_install_MetaMask"}),(0,s.jsxs)("h3",{children:["2. Get some ETH ",(0,s.jsx)("img",{src:"/img/logos/ETH.svg",className:"emoji"})]}),"To make any transactions on the Ethereum network, you need some of its native currency called Ether or $ETH.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"If you already own other cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin, you can swap them for ETH on an exchange like ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://FixedFloat.com/BTC/ETH?ref=".concat(n.gi),target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"FixedFloat"}),". This doesn't require any registration or personal information.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"If you don't own any cryptocurrency yet, you can buy some with fiat currency (USD, EUR, etc.) on an exchange like ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://bitstamp.net",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Bitstamp"}),".The registration process for Bitstamp is somewhat complex, involving KYC (\"Know Your Customer\") which means you'll have to send them selfies and photos of your government ID. If you're okay with paying higher fees (around 8% instead of <1%) to buy your first few ETH, you can also use the official ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/buy",className:"tl",children:"HEX Credit Card on-ramp"}),".",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Alternative: Coinbase instead of Bitstamp"}),"1. ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://help.coinbase.com/en/coinbase/getting-started/getting-started-with-coinbase/create-a-coinbase-account",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Create a Coinbase account"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"2. Fund your Coinbase account with fiat currency (",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://help.coinbase.com/en/pro/managing-my-account/funding-your-account/funding-your-account-with-usd",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"USD"})," / ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://help.coinbase.com/en/pro/managing-my-account/funding-your-account/funding-your-account-with-eur",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"EUR"})," / ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://help.coinbase.com/en/pro/managing-my-account/funding-your-account/funding-your-account-with-gbp",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"GBP"}),")",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"3. ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://coinbase.com/how-to-buy/ethereum",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Buy ETH"}),(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Additional Resources"}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/security",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Official recommendations regarding security"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://cryptocoffee369.medium.com/how-to-buy-hex-cryptocurrency-94b456f8d832",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"How to buy ETH / HEX: step by step"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/_assets/vids/HEX_how_to_buy_ETH.mp4",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"How to buy ETH with Credit Card (alternative via Wyre)"})]})},{title:"Get started with HEX",subtitle:"Learn how to buy some HEX and start your first stake",slug:"hex",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["You can also buy HEX directly, but you'll need ETH eventually for staking or sending HEX. It's important to keep some ETH (~$10) for future gas fees.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"How to swap with HEXscout"}),"HEXscout Swap always guarantees the best possible swap rates by combining the liquidity of many different DEXs. Simply make sure you have at least ~$50 of ETH in your MetaMask wallet, then connect it to ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/stake",className:"tl",children:"HEXscout Swap"}),".",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Plan your first HEX stake"}),"The concept behind HEX is earning trustless interest by locking up your HEX for fixed periods of time. Staking is optional, but liquid HEX can be diluted over time by inflation.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"If you've never started a HEX stake before, try starting a small stake that only lasts a couple of days. You can even stake for a single day. This won't be profitable, as you'll have to pay gas fees for starting and ending your stakes. Because your stakes earn interest in HEX every day they are active, small/short stakes usually don't generate enough interest to cover the gas costs. Once you're comfortable with the process, you can consider starting longer stakes.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"How to start a new stake with HEXscout"}),"First, make sure you own some liquid HEX and ETH to pay for gas fees. Then, open the ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/stake",className:"tl",children:"Staking Page"}),".",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"To start your first stake, you need to set 2 parameters:",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"1. How many HEX do you want to stake?",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"2. How long should your stake last? The minimum is 1 day, the maximum 5555 days (~15 years).",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"After confirming your new stake, you'll have to wait a few seconds for the Ethereum blockchain to confirm your transaction.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"That's it. Congratulations, you're now a staked Hexican!"]})},{title:"Ladder my stakes",subtitle:"Learn about the right laddering techniques for you",slug:"ladder",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["If you've never started a HEX stake before, try starting a small stake that only lasts a couple of days to get comfortable with the process. Once you're comfortable with the mechanics, consider starting longer stakes.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),'You can combine multiple HEX stakes into a "Ladder" with different strategies to optimize risk/reward based on your personal preferences. There is no one-size-fits-all staking strategy - the best choice depends on your personal circumstances, goals, and preferences. The following strategies are just ideas to help you build your own personal Ladder.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Linear"}),"To start a Linear Staking Ladder, split your HEX into equal portions and stake them for a linearly increasing number of days.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: Split 1M HEX into portions of 100K and stake them until your next 10 birthdays. That would be a Linear Ladder of 1M HEX in 1-year intervals.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Paycheck"}),"To start a Paycheck Staking Ladder, split your HEX into equal parts and stake them until the beginning of each month. After ending a stake, restake the principle to continue your ladder. This way it's never-ending.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: Split 1M HEX into 36 portions and stake them over the next 3 years. Once the first stake ends after 30 days, restake it for 3 years. This way the Ladder will always be evenly distributed over the coming 3 years.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Disclaimer: Gas fees on Ethereum can be expensive. If you start a new stake with HEXscout, you'll see the estimated gas costs for starting and ending the stake before committing. Consider whether it's worthwhile to stake monthly. Alternatively, you could build a quarterly or yearly ladder. This way you have fewer stakes, lower gas costs, and less effort because you have to restake less often.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Longterm"}),"If you're comfortable with the mechanics of starting and ending stakes and are confident in the ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/security",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"security"})," of your wallet, consider long-term stakes (5-15 years).",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Pros: These stakes pay exceptionally well due to the high LongerPaysBetter bonus. Long stakes also protect you from selling HEX too early.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Cons: You'll have less flexibility to react to potential volatility. To counter this, you could combine a long-term ladder with using a portion of your HEX to buy short-term /pooled stakes.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: Stake 300K HEX for 5 years, 500K for 10 years and 200K for 15 years.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Pooled Stakes Timing"}),"The MAXIMUS DAO Pooled Stakes will be released every 1, 3, 5, 10, and 15 years. You might want to ladder your stakes according to their end dates so you can frontrun them. They're likely to be bearish events for the HEX price, so you might want to take profits before the horde of stakers does. If you're not interested in taking profits, you might still want to join them to receive a higher BiggerPaysBetter Bonus. In either case, you should end your stakes a couple of days to weeks before theirs run out.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: The first TRIO stake ends on 13th October 2025. You could make sure one of your ladder's stakes ends on the 1st October 2025, two weeks earlier. This might allow you to frontrun a potential sell-off. You'll also have liquid HEX to mint new TRIO during the redemption phase.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"5555"}),"Stake a fixed portion of your HEX for the maximum duration of 5555 days (~15.2 years). This will ensure you receive the maximum LongerPaysBetter Bonus of 200%. Stake the rest according to your personal preferences.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: Before starting a new Ladder, set aside 20% of your HEX for a single 5555 stake.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Binomial"}),"If you're using HEX to save up for a specific event in the future but aren't sure about the exact point in time when it will happen, you can plan your stakes to end around that event. Split your HEX into a few portions, stake the largest one close to the event, and some smaller ones before and after.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Pros: You gain maximum flexibility around the event while hedging against volatility.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Example: You want to use HEX stakes to help save for your kid's college tuition, which is due in about 5-7 years. You'll also need some money every year to pay for running costs, but you don't know the exact timeframe. You could build a ladder by staking 10% of your HEX for 3 years, 12% for 4, 18% for 5, 20% for 6, 18% for 7, 12% for 8, and 10% for 9."]})},{title:"Use alternative Staking Methods",subtitle:"Learn how to level up your Staking game",slug:"staking",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["Help! There are so many ways to stake my HEX, which is the right one?",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"During the last 3 years a considerable ecosystem has been developed around HEX. It's easy to lose track of the various options for investing in HEX. Here is a break down of what advantages and disadvantages they offer for your goals:",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Native"}),"+ The only official way to stake. The others were built by the community and are not officially endorsed.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"+ By far the most secure and battle-tested way, with two independent security audits. Stakers interact directly with the HEX smart contract, which has been running flawlessly for multiple years. There are no middlemen or third-party contracts involved.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),'- "Non-transferable", meaning that native stakes are tied to the wallet they were started from. There is no possibility to transfer ownership to another wallet while they are active. You have to make sure your wallet will stay ',(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/security",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"secure"}),"for the entire duration of its stakes.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"- The gas fees for ending a stake on Ethereum can be expensive, especially for multi-year long stakes. In the last bull run, some Hexicans had to pay more than $1000 in gas fees to end a single stake.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Encapsulated"}),'A community-built smart contract called "Hedron" enables anyone to stake HEX as a "Hedron Stake Instance" (HSI). This starts an encapsulated HEX stake and mints a NFT at the same time. The NFT is transferable and tradable. The NFT\'s current owner can end the stake once it is mature and receive the staked HEX + yield.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"+ Flexibility, as encapsulation enables you to transfer or auction off ownership before the underlying stake matures.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"+ Hedron has been in existence for a few months without any problems. The smart contract appears to be secure.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"- Fewer frontends support HSIs compared to native stakes (yet). Because Hedron is a relatively new alternative, there is simply less infrastructure. This is not a serious problem for most users though.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Pooled Stakes"}),"Pooled Stakes are a type of investment opportunity introduced by Maximus DAO. They allow you to pool your HEX stakes together with others and mint a placeholder token in return. This token is transferable and tradeable and represents your share of the underlying HEX stakes. Maximus DAO offers five different stakes: 1 (BASE), 3 (TRIO), 5 (LUCKY), 10 (DECI), and 15 (MAXI) years long. At the end of each stake, participants have 14 days to redeem their HEX + interest by burning their placeholder token. If they do not redeem their tokens, the underlying HEX + interest will be automatically restaked for the same period. New participants can join during this period.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"+ Flexibility: You can transfer or sell the tokens at any time.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"+ The BiggerPaysBetter bonus is higher when you participate in a pooled stake than when you stake alone. However, note that half of the bonus and all accumulated HDRN are sent to the Maximus TEAM Contract instead of the token holders.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"-Low liquidity: Buying and selling tokens on the open market can be difficult, leading to high slippage, especially for larger orders. - Delayed price correlation: The price of the Pooled Stake Tokens is not closely tied to the price of HEX. You can check the current premiums/discounts at the ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/buy",className:"tl",children:"Market"})," Pooled Stakes table",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"- Risk of endstaking or restaking failure: There is a small risk that endstaking or restaking will not work, as it will be done for the first time in 2023 and has only been tested on Testnet."]})},{title:"Make sure to not commit Tax Fraud",subtitle:"Learn how to file HEX related Tax Reports in your jurisdiction",slug:"tax",content:"Coming soon!"},{title:"Spread awareness about HEX",subtitle:"Learn about how to promote your bag of HEX most efficiently",slug:"marketing",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["Once you have acquired your first HEX, you can increase their value by spreading the word about HEX.COM. There are a few different ways you can do this:",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Onboard your friends & family"}),"The easiest way to spread awareness about HEX is by word of mouth. Tell you friends, ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/faq/#mother",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"mother"})," & colleagues about it.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Onboard your followers"}),"If you are interested in becoming a public figure for HEX, you can build your own sub-community by streaming, producing videos, answering questions, and helping new users to get into the ecosystem. Spread the word by commenting on social media platforms such as Twitter and ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://t.me/HEXcrypto",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Telegram"}),'. Make sure to always include the iconic "HEX.COM" link.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Remember, there are very few actually good things in this world that you could recommend to your followers, and HEX is one of them. By promoting HEX, you can not only increase the value of your own stack, but also help others to benefit from it. It's a win-win situation for everyone!",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Spend money on marketing"}),'Altruism is great, but for pure return on investment (ROI), it is usually better to just buy HEX. The following advice mostly applies to "whales" who already own "enough" HEX.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"To pay for any kind of HEX advertisement, it is best to use external money. Don't sell your HEX to buy ads, as it drives the price down (which also affects the rest of your HEX holdings).",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),'Richard Heart has taught us that direct marketing wins. Measurable performance, such as "did the ad get clicked/did the conversion work," is important.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"The most efficient and easiest way is to donate crypto to ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://HEXpostcards.com",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"HEXpostcards"}),", a community initiative that has already sent hundreds of thousands of postcard ads to wealthy Americans. You can donate ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/0x716b1e629b0d3abd14bd1e9e6557cdfaee839668",className:"tl",children:"USDC"})," or ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/0x25d4cceba035aabb7ac79c4f2fead5bc74e6b9d8",className:"tl",children:"ETH/USDT"}),".",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Another creative way is to buy Super Chats (on YouTube) or donations (on Twitch) during large streams to advertise HEX. Depending on the stream, this can result in a great cost-per-thousand impressions (CPM). You can also buy (unofficial) merchandise and stickers from ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://HEXmerch.com",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"HEXmerch.com"}),".",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"SciVice's (Richard Heart's book) \"Benefits of Marketing\" paragraph"}),"\"[...] It shouldn't work for more than just promoting Bitcoin. But it's easier to do that because people see financial gain. Such as, put in 0.5% of your holdings, do this marketing campaign, watch the new money come in, and see your wealth grow. You could even sell into the new money and make back your $5,000 and roll it again, and roll it again, and roll it again. And that's how marketing works. Your lifetime value of customer exceeds your cost of acquisition, and you're rolling in the dough. If searched for, many of the habits and inclinations we have can probably be traced to a hardcore marketing campaign.\"",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Additional Resources"}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://youtube.com/watch?v=LvNftMFACvI",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Richard Heart about buying ads for HEX"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://twitter.com/RichardHeartWin/status/1598050159375814657",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Richard Heart about marketing"})," (direct mail good, digital/sports bad. UBS + URL wins)",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/faq/#five-year-old",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"How to explain HEX to a five-year-old"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/downloads",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Official marketing material"})]})},{title:"Get better DEX order execution",subtitle:"Learn how you can get more HEX for less money",slug:"trade",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["Most of HEX's ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/wiki/liquidity",className:"tl",children:"liquidity"})," is on Uniswap V2 and V3. The official Uniswap frontend combines both of these, but ignores other liquidity sources such as SushiSwap, ShibaSwap, Mooniswap, and DODO, among others. ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/wiki/1inch",className:"tl",children:"1inch"})," is another decentralized protocol that spreads your orders across all available liquidity sources. This results in less slippage, especially for larger trades.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"You can also use the ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://help.1inch.io/en/articles/6796085-what-is-1inch-fusion-and-how-does-it-work",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"1inch Fusion Mode"})," to trade the most popular tokens without having to pay gas fees. This works by providing liquidity for a short period of time (3 or 10 minutes) and waiting for somebody else to trade on your liquidity.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"You can ",(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/swap",className:"tl",children:"interact with the 1inch protocol through HEXscout"}),". This guarantees you the best possible price for your trades.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"If you are planning to buy/sell more than $1M of HEX, it is smart to split your trade into multiple orders. You can do this manually by waiting a bit between each trade, or you can use a limit order protocol such as ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://matcha.xyz/markets/1/0x2b591e99afe9f32eaa6214f7b7629768c40eeb39/0xa0b86991c6218b36c1d19d4a2e9eb0ce3606eb48",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Matcha"}),"."]})},{title:"Set up institutional grade storage",subtitle:"Learn how to secure large amounts of crypto by utilizing multi-sig",slug:"storage",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["If you are starting native HEX stakes, it is important to ensure that you are the only one who has access to your wallet during the entire time your stakes are active. For example, if you start a 15-year long stake, you'll need to make sure your wallet remains secure for the next 15 years.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"It is also important to consider the possibility of a significant increase in the value of your staked HEX. For example, if you start a 10-year long stake of $1000 worth of HEX now, you should secure your wallet as if it contains hundreds of thousands of dollars' worth of HEX. This will help protect your investment in the event that the value of HEX increases significantly.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Use Hardware Wallets"}),"If you plan to store more than $10,000 worth of crypto, we recommend that you get a hardware wallet. These wallets are much more secure than any kind of software wallet. Most hardware wallets can be connected to MetaMask and HEXscout. Here is a guide on how to set up and use a hardware wallet:",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"1) Buy a ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://shop.trezor.io/product/trezor-one-black",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Trezor Model One"})," (roughly $70)",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),'2) Once your Trezor arrives, follow the directions and set it up. During the setup process, write down the "Secret Recovery Phrase" that is shown to you by hand with a pen on a physical piece of paper. Store this piece of paper in a different location from your Trezor, such as a safe deposit box at your bank or in the house of a trusted friend or family member.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"3) Download the ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://MetaMask.io/download",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"MetaMask browser extension"}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"4) Connect your Trezor to MetaMask",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"5) Send a small amount of ETH to your Trezor (the Ethereum address shown within MetaMask)",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"6) Try sending the amount back to another wallet you own to test if your Trezor works and you set up everything correctly",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"7) Connect your MetaMask to HEXscout to manage your liquid assets & HEX stakes",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Use a separate storage address"}),"Smart contracts such as Uniswap often require the permission of your address to spend ERC20 tokens on your behalf. However, there is always a minimal risk that these contracts could be exploited, resulting in the loss of your tokens. Additionally, some hardware wallets may not display all the impacts of a transaction before you sign it. Even signing text messages can carry risks.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"To mitigate these risks, you can use a separate address solely for storage. The only transactions you should sign from this address are those to send assets. For trading assets, claiming airdrops, or signing text messages, use different addresses.",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Multi-sig"}),"If you own more than $1M worth of crypto, you should not rely on a single hardware wallet, as it represents a single centralized point of failure. While hardware wallets are still incredibly secure for storing crypto if used correctly, a more advanced approach for storing larger amounts of crypto is to use a multi-sig setup. This requires MULTIple wallets to SIGn off on every transaction. While this approach is slightly more complex than using a single hardware wallet, it is worth it for storing larger amounts of crypto, especially for long-term storage like 5555 stakes.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"The easiest way to accomplish this for web3 chains (such as Ethereum, BSC, Polygon, and PulseChain) is with ",(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://gnosis-safe.io",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Gnosis Safe"}),'. Gnosis is a factory for special smart contracts called "Safes" that work like normal Ethereum accounts, but with distributed ownership. For example, you could set up a safe that requires signatures from three out of five geographically distributed hardware wallets to spend funds.',(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),'Gnosis also allows you to transfer ownership of your Safes, including all of their HEX stakes. This means that even native HEX stakes are transferable, although they are harder to sell compared to HSIs. Seting up a Gnosis Safe can be a little bit challenging. In case you need any help we are happy to assist you with our "Wallet" ',(0,s.jsx)(o.Z,{href:"/support",className:"tl",children:"Support Package"}),"!",(0,s.jsx)("h3",{children:"Additional Resources"}),(0,s.jsx)("a",{href:"https://hex.com/security",target:"_blank",className:"tl",children:"Official recommendations regarding security"})]})},{title:"Invest at an institutional level",subtitle:"Learn how to get exposure to HEX's price appreciation within legacy finance as an accredited investor",slug:"trust",content:(0,s.jsxs)(s.Fragment,{children:["If you are an accredited investor, you may be able to use the (unofficial) HEX Investment Trust™, a registered 506(c) private trust, to gain exposure to HEX's price appreciation.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),"Please note that the HEX Investment Trust is an unofficial product and should be thoroughly researched before making any investment decisions. It is important to carefully consider the risks and potential rewards of any investment, and to consult with a financial advisor or legal counsel before making any investment decisions.",(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)("br",{}),(0,s.jsx)(r.Z,{src:"HEXscout_What_is_the_HEX_Investment_Trust"})]})}]},25893:function(){}}]);